## 13  L8396 "§30.3.3 completes this reading" — the TARGET READ, not token-probed
   L8456  ### 30.3.3 What the interval machinery was
   L8457   Chapter-length work went into C1P, monotone endpoints and PQ-trees, and the d = 2
   L8458   characterisation is proved there: X is reorderable iff every row is an interval with both endpoints
   L8459   monotone, iff no interval nests strictly inside another. Four lemmas, three verified independently —
   L8460   2,047, 3,751 and 20,000 instances — with Booth & Lueker's linear PQ-tree construction cited
   L8461   for the fourth.
   L8462  
   L8463   **The fourth lemma, verified.** The three lemmas above were checked at 2,047, 3,751 and 20,000
   L8464   instances; the fourth stood on Booth and Lueker's construction and on nothing of this book's own.
   L8465   It is now discharged, and it did not need a linear-time algorithm:
   L8466  
   L8467      A set of intervals admits an ordering in which both endpoints are non-decreasing **iff** no
   L8468      interval nests strictly inside another. Sort by left endpoint; if a right endpoint then
   L8469      decreases, the later interval has the weakly greater left end and the strictly smaller right
   L8470      end, so it nests strictly. Conversely a strictly nesting pair admits no such order. ∎
   L8471  
   L8472   Verified exhaustively over all 2,354 interval sets of two to four intervals on ground sets of two to
   L8473   five points: zero counterexamples. **Strictly** is load-bearing — an interval sharing an endpoint
   L8474   with its container does not nest strictly, and reading it as ordinary containment refutes the lemma
   L8475   on 1,098 of those 2,354 sets. That reading was tried first here and was wrong, which is the whole
   L8476   reason the qualifier is in the statement. Register 247.
   L8477  
   L8478        That apparatus is a REPRESENTATION of a 2-colouring. It is correct and it is not the reason d =
   L8479        2 is easy. The reason is that two cells in two dimensions differ on at most two axes.
   L8480  

